NAME
    qemu-published-test.sh - visually test the published m-boot USB image
                             on BIOS x86_64 and both UEFI architectures

SYNOPSIS
    tests/qemu-published-test.sh
        [--target all|i386-pc|x86_64-efi|arm64-efi]
        [--output DIR] [--verify-only]

DESCRIPTION
    Validates the exact images/m-boot-combined.raw.gz distribution that
    usb-install.sh flashes onto physical media. Checks SHA256 of the
    compressed image, checks that its metadata requires the complete
    loader on the ESP, decompresses to one private sparse 2 GiB raw image
    under DIR and validates its size and raw SHA256. This requires GNU dd
    and enough host filesystem space/quota for the sparse raw image.
    DIR defaults to the current working directory (NOT /tmp).
    The temporary image and directory are removed when the test exits.

    Runs the existing tests/qemu-run.sh sequentially on the SAME image:
        i386-pc      x86_64 legacy BIOS
        x86_64-efi   x86_64 UEFI (OVMF)
        arm64-efi    ARM64 UEFI (AAVMF/EDK2)

    Each QEMU launch uses snapshot mode and separate temporary UEFI
    variables. No mounted device, host disk, USB stick or physical
    partition is accessed. Root is not needed; GRUB and images are not
    rebuilt. The raw source is rehashed after every QEMU instance.

    For each platform inspect the graphical GRUB m-loader menu and its
    "Inspect boot context" entry. Close the QEMU window, then type PASS
    or FAIL in the terminal. QEMU exiting successfully does not by itself
    prove that the loader booted. The command exits nonzero if any
    platform fails or the operator does not confirm it.

OPTIONS
    --target        Default all. Limit to one target when needed.
    --output DIR    Existing writable directory with suitable disk quota
                    for a sparse image; defaults to the current directory.
    --verify-only   Verify the real gzip/raw image without starting QEMU,
                    without requiring a terminal; useful for CI.
    --help          Show usage.

REQUIREMENTS
    Linux with POSIX sh, GNU dd (iflag=fullblock, conv=sparse), gzip,
    sha256sum, and enough free file quota for the sparse temporary disk.
    Interactive runs need qemu-system-x86_64 and qemu-system-aarch64,
    and matching OVMF/AAVMF CODE+VARS firmware at the standard locations
    recognized by tests/qemu-run.sh. A graphical display is necessary
    to inspect the GRUB menu. No sudo is required.

EXAMPLES
    cd /path/to/m-boot
    ./tests/qemu-published-test.sh

    ./tests/qemu-published-test.sh --target arm64-efi --output "$HOME"
    ./tests/qemu-published-test.sh --verify-only

LIMITATIONS
    The QEMU source is the published unexpanded 2 GiB disk image, not the
    physical USB stick with its enlarged exFAT data partition. It checks
    the same boot partitions/loader payload as the flashed image but
    DOES NOT verify real USB firmware boot or physical device readability.
    Automated checksum/preparation PASS does not imply successful QEMU
    firmware boot: visual inspection and the operator's explicit per-target
    PASS are required. Secure Boot and ISO boot are not verified.

